@startuml activity-fr-09
' Report §2.1 — FR-09 Release seats on payment failure or hold expiry.
' Source: PaymentEventConsumers.paymentFailed, RegistrationApplicationService.cancelUnpaid
' and expireOverdue, Registration.cancel/expire/isExpiredAt, HoldExpirySweeper.sweep,
' SessionView.release.
' Second pass (FR-10): seats-released will also promote the head of the session's waitlist.
!include include/style.iuml
!include include/activity.iuml

title FR-09 — Release seats on payment failure or hold expiry

|registration-service|
start
:payment-failed<
note right: compensation path 1 — the charge was refused (FR-07)
:PaymentEventConsumers.paymentFailed;
if (eventId already in processed_events?) then (yes)
  :ignore the redelivery;
  stop
else (no)
endif
:record eventId in processed_events;
:RegistrationApplicationService.cancelUnpaid(registrationId);
if (registration found and still
PENDING_PAYMENT?) then (no)
  :log a warning and drop;
  stop
else (yes)
endif
:Registration.cancel()
each HELD SeatHold → RELEASED,
record SeatsReleased per hold,
status → CANCELLED,
record RegistrationCancelled;
:save → regdb.registrations, seat_holds,
return seats: SessionView.release(quantity)
→ regdb.session_views;
:after commit, StreamBridge sends;
|Kafka|
$EVT:seats-released ×N
key: sessionId>
$EVT:registration-cancelled
key: registrationId>
stop

|registration-service|
start
:time event: HoldExpirySweeper.sweep()
every sweep-interval (PT10S)<
note right: compensation path 2 — nobody paid in time
:RegistrationApplicationService.expireOverdue(now)
loads every PENDING_PAYMENT registration;
:keep those with any SeatHold
where now is after expiresAt;
if (any overdue?) then (no)
  :nothing to release;
  stop
else (yes)
endif
repeat
  :Registration.expire()
  each HELD SeatHold → RELEASED,
  record SeatsReleased per hold,
  status → EXPIRED,
  record RegistrationExpired;
  :save, and return seats to SessionView;
repeat while (more overdue registrations?) is (yes) not (no)
:after the sweep's single commit, StreamBridge sends;
|Kafka|
$EVT:seats-released ×N
key: sessionId>
$EVT:registration-expired
key: registrationId>
stop

note right
  The hold window is configuration:
  conference.registration.hold-window
  is PT2M for demos (15 minutes is the
  stated business rule).
  A free registration is never
  PENDING_PAYMENT, so never expires.
  Cancelled and expired are separate
  events so the M3 funnel can count
  failure and abandonment apart.
end note
@enduml
